let's take a quick look at how to use  the Google cloud sequel proxy go to  cloud google.com and open up your cloud  console go to the sequel section here  you can see your cloud sequel instances  if you don't have a cloud sequel  instance you can create one click your  instance to be taken to the instance  overview page now go to the access  control tab and then go to the users tab  specify a new root password go to the  following page to follow along with the  rest of the tutorial scroll down and  click enable the API choose your project  and click continue the API should now be  enabled follow the installation  instructions for your operating system  now run g-cloud auth application default  loggin go back to the sequel overview  page and copy the instant connection  name run the cloud sequel proxy and pass  in your instance connection name at the  end of the string you also want type in  equal to TCP : 3 3 0 6 you now have a  direct connection to cloud sequel  through the local proxy
 

